No, it doesn't.  If, for instance, a gnome has an attack wand and is
far away, you can survive the first blast and duck upstairs (even a /
death might miss you).  A mind flayer might appear on any level in the
mines.  Dwarves with mithril and broad picks can sometimes present a
hazard even to Valks with decent AC at this stage of the game.  Orcs
with poison arrows might appear, requiring a hasty retreat if you lack
MC3 and PR.

All kinds of things make it a valuable strategy, and some of them
aren't solved by high hp and damage output and low AC.



